\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Recycling-induced sharpening and its derived mitigation (Countdown, tier 1).} \emph  {(a)} Three seeds, both axes: recycling (B2) buys mean@16 with $\text  {pass@}16$ coverage. On this tier the moderate gate (B3) gives back most of the mean without moving coverage --- tier-1 destinations saturate early, so admitted relabels are few --- while full-strength gating (corrected decay, 1 seed) returns coverage \emph  {above} baseline at the mean's full price: gate strength is a dial along the trade, and its useful middle lives on the frontier tier, where the same moderate setting restores coverage to baseline ($.279{\pm }.019$ vs.\ $.274$) keeping $\sim $60\% of the mean gain (\S  7.6). \emph  {(b)} The mechanism in-run: the gate's rejection rate rises monotonically as the model's reachable set saturates its relabel destinations, while the ungated dose rides its cap. \emph  {(c)} Gated recycling preserves \emph  {more} policy entropy than no recycling --- admitted relabels are a spread-preserving gradient.}}{10}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sharpening}{{7}{10}{\textbf {Recycling-induced sharpening and its derived mitigation (Countdown, tier 1).} \emph {(a)} Three seeds, both axes: recycling (B2) buys mean@16 with $\passat {16}$ coverage. On this tier the moderate gate (B3) gives back most of the mean without moving coverage --- tier-1 destinations saturate early, so admitted relabels are few --- while full-strength gating (corrected decay, 1 seed) returns coverage \emph {above} baseline at the mean's full price: gate strength is a dial along the trade, and its useful middle lives on the frontier tier, where the same moderate setting restores coverage to baseline ($.279{\pm }.019$ vs.\ $.274$) keeping $\sim $60\% of the mean gain (\S 7.6). \emph {(b)} The mechanism in-run: the gate's rejection rate rises monotonically as the model's reachable set saturates its relabel destinations, while the ungated dose rides its cap. \emph {(c)} Gated recycling preserves \emph {more} policy entropy than no recycling --- admitted relabels are a spread-preserving gradient}{figure.7}{}}
